  },
  {
    "description": "Measure a video's picture, as a colourist reads the scopes, since you can't judge a grade from a few stills: mean and 5th to 95th percentile luma, the histogram's shadows, mids and highlights, crushed blacks and clipped whites, mean saturation, and how far skin sits from the skin-tone line. Each number comes with what a graded picture usually shows. \`from\`/\`to\` (seconds) measure one stretch; it samples up to 60 frames. Grade with \`effect\`s, render, and measure again.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "every": {
