    "name": "scopes",
  },
  {
    "description": "Measure a file's sound, since you can't listen to it: integrated loudness (aim for -14 LUFS), loudness range, true and sample peak (clipping), and noise floor. With speech: how much of it is speech, and how far under the voice the sound between phrases sits (music under speech: 18 to 24 dB under) and how much of the 1 to 4 kHz speech band it fills. The beat (tempo and where beats fall, to cut on) when there's a steady one: measure the music file itself, since speech over it hides the beat; and the sections where the energy changes for a while. \`from\`/\`to\` (seconds) measure one stretch; times come back from the start of the file.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "from": {
