      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "audio_stats",
  },
  {
    "description": "Background music written as code, with no samples to license: \`script\` is a generator, a .js module whose \`export default function (ctx, params)\` schedules sound on \`ctx\`, an OfflineAudioContext as long as \`duration\`, with Web Audio nodes (oscillators, filters, gains, buffers of noise, convolvers). It runs in the pinned headless Chrome, in a sandbox with no network. \`params\` has duration, sampleRate (48000), seed, and the tempo, key and energy given here, for the generator to read. Math.random is seeded from \`seed\`, so the same arguments make the same track (Chrome's mixer can round the last bits differently between runs, never audibly). Saves a 48 kHz stereo WAV at \`out\`, brought to -14 LUFS with its peaks held, and never overwrites. Use it as one of render's \`audio\` tracks (volume about 0.1 to 0.2 under speech, \`duck: true\`). The plugin's generators and how to choose one are in guide("music").",
